
!.env.example
!.vscode/extensions.json
# (decision D6, ssot/09-runbooks/secrets-rotation.md).
# ---- Data / dumps ------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- Node / pnpm -------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- Personal / never commit -------------------------------------------------
# ---- Prisma ------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- Python (EDMC plugin) ----------------------------------------------------
# ---- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- Vendored upstream -------------------------------------------------------
# Cloned and pinned at build time, not committed (ssot/05-integrations/coriolis.md).
# Galaxy dumps are multi-GB. Never commit one.
# Generated client only. Migrations ARE committed.
# Production secrets live in a root-owned 0600 .env ON THE SERVER, never here
# Your own working notes. Safe to put IDs, keys and half-finished thoughts in.
*-credentials.json
*.dump
*.key
*.local.md
*.log
*.p12
*.pem
*.pfx
*.py[cod]
*.sql.gz
*.swp
*.tsbuildinfo
*~
.DS_Store
.cloudflared/
.env
.env.*
.idea/
.next/
.notes/
.pnpm-store/
.turbo/
.venv/
.vscode/*
TODO.local.md
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
apps/api/.env
build/
# ★ EXCEPT THE COMPANION'S SOURCE ICONS ★
#
# `build/` above is unanchored, so it matches at ANY depth — including
# apps/companion/build/, which is not build output at all. It holds the squadron
# badge that electron-builder reads for the app icon, the taskbar icon, the tray
# icon and the installer icon on all three platforms.
#
# They were therefore never committed, and CI failed on a runner that had no
# such file: `ENOENT: lstat 'build/tray.png'`. It worked locally for the one
# reason that matters least — the files were sitting there untracked.
!apps/companion/build/
!apps/companion/build/**
coverage/
credentials.json
data/
desktop.ini
dist/
galaxy*.json*
next-env.d.ts
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
out/
packages/db/.env
packages/db/generated/
pnpm-debug.log*
prisma/generated/
uploads/
vendor/coriolis-data/
vendor/coriolis/
venv/
wg*.conf

# Encrypted secret backups — never committed, even encrypted.
*.tar.gz.enc
grims-secrets-*
restored-secrets/

# Recovery material. These live OUTSIDE the repo by design (the recovery card is
# written to the user's home directory), but a copy pasted in here would be the
# single worst thing this repository could contain: the vault passphrase opens
# both the secrets vault and every database backup.
GRIMS-SQUAD-RECOVERY.txt
*RECOVERY*.txt
grims-vault-passphrase*
*.enc
vault-*.enc

# Verification builds. Kept OUT of .next so a build cannot disturb a running
# dev server — see apps/web/next.config.mjs.
.next-check/

# Packaged desktop builds. electron-builder writes the entire Electron runtime
# here — a few hundred megabytes of Chromium per platform, none of which is
# ours and all of which is reproducible from source. Releases are built by CI
# and attached as workflow artifacts.
apps/companion/release/
.local-storage/

# Operations credentials (Cloudflare token, etc). Never in git, per the standing secrets rule.
.secrets/
